Evidence E - the reviewer's probe (supertest, same jest.mock line as the PR's test, test database seeded with 214 courses, 37 of them drafts; q shown decoded):
GET /courses/search?q=react          200  4 courses, all "published"
GET /courses/search?q=' OR '1'='1    200  20 courses, 6 with "status": "draft"
GET /courses/search?q=don't          200  []   (the seed has "Don't Repeat Yourself: Refactoring TypeScript", published)
GET /courses/search?q=%              200  20 courses   (no title contains "%")
API log during the probe: no lines

Statement: "The search text becomes part of the SQL: for ' OR '1'='1 the WHERE clause reads title ILIKE '%' OR '1'='1%' AND status = 'published', and because AND binds tighter than OR, every course whose title matches '%' comes back, drafts included."

